{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501429-metaplot-plot-thread-reboot","id":1501429,"title":"Metaplot Plot-Thread Reboot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-26T15:06:25-08:00","id":1501429,"title":"Metaplot Plot-Thread Reboot","content":"I think most people who frequent these forums regularly know that the Metaplot of our favorite gothic punk RPGs can be controversial, but I like to think that largely comes from a place of affection.<br /> <br /> That said, here\u2019s the idea I had that led me to make this thread: I like the idea of having a bunch of little dials, optional threads, and story packages that I can use as I please for my games. This has come up with my admiration for the Scion 2e Companion book and the administration I\u2019ve felt and seen others express for those books which contain optional threads one can implement in their game setting as a means to progress the world.<br /> <br /> IMO these threads and stories help to prevent the setting from feeling static and create all sorts of little ways that one can use them as inspiration for a story.<br /> <br /> So, here\u2019s the idea: you have a blank document in front of you and the setting\u2019s clock has been rolled back to 1991-1992. You can have as much or as little knowledge of what would be added to the setting in later books as you want. What sort of things do you put into the document as options. <br /> <br /> Here\u2019s some examples of my own:<br /> <br /> \u2022The Hag and the Wall<br /> -With the dissolution of the USSR the domains which have answered to the Brujah Council in Moscow for 3/4rs of a century are suddenly sundered from one another. The power scramble has begun. Every domain sees its own domestic claimants for prince come out of the woodwork. The Brujah Justicar Carlak has been planning for this moment for years and he\u2019s moving quickly to get the kindred in his corner seats in prominent domains - by the time this is all over he plans to be the key power player in the former eastern bloc. The Ordea League is raising its own clarion call and seeking to see the old domains restored and furthermore to parcel off new territory for their broods; they\u2019ve cooperated with the Camarilla against the Anarchs and Sabbat for this long and they\u2019re calling in favors. The Mikaelites who fled Greece in the final nights of Byzantium see this as the perfect opportunity - now is the time to restore the third Rome and to rekindle the embers of Mikael\u2019s Dream. Meanwhile, while all these powers scheme and most kindred are scrambling simply to survive, The Great Hag has risen from her torporous slumber and seeks to create a dark empire of her own - one decorated with the ashen remains of her so-called clan mates\u2026<br /> (I personally don\u2019t like the Shadow Curtain and feel that the Baba Yaga plot is more interesting without it.)<br /> <br /> \u2022The domains around the Great Lakes our the heart of the North American Camarilla and embody the sect\u2019s status quo on that continent. Lodin and all the other powers that be in those Midwestern cities want to keep it that way. Yet their are threats at every corner. On one hand the Anarchs have never been driven totally underground in Chicago and every year it seems that the Black Prince or some new upstart has more followers. Furthermore every concession made to keep the peace one more night, however slight, smacks Justicar Petrodon as the gravest display of weakness seen yet and the princes of the lakes suspect that if Petrodon had his way he would bury them all and have them replaced by the broods of old world princes. The Lupines who flock to the lakes from all over the continent certainly aren\u2019t making matters any easier, nor are the Sabbat packs who come prowling out of Detroit or Smiling Jack\u2019s free riders from out west. The domains of the Great Lakes have to be careful, lest the tentative balance maintained in the American Camarilla Heartlands is overthrown\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T15:39:31-08:00","id":1501432,"title":"","content":"This is similar to what our gm has told us when we asked about our current plot where in our campaign the ucrain madness is basically GRU is deadly afraid of another vampire of calibre of baba yaga so they started this attrocity so they can draw out this millenia old vampire.<br /> <br /> Originally our GM had the idea that the ventrue prince of Trier who whas embraced back then in the second city made an alliance with the kiever rus by marrying the child of the prince of Kiew during 1000 who where embraced just to give him a wife. Now 1000 years later the fledgeling became a methusalah herself and sired daughters too. While the world may have forgotten the prince of trier still remembers the pledge he made. Now as the ukraine is oppressed he helps his with in supporting her that her eldest daughter could become the next prince of kiew and our characters who still had an undead debt to fullfill to him should go in there too and help her to become the winner in this fight and when there is chances help the oppressed population too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T02:56:08-08:00","id":1501453,"title":"","content":"My suggestion for metaplot reboot is that gehenna was cancelled after two of the 3rd got vacumn bomber in 2000 (ravnos and tzmisce) intiating the 2nd inquisition. This allows for a more stable ongoing setting. I'll do a write up on how this affects the sects later. I've also been playing with getting the anarchs a cohesive idea of what they want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T05:22:36-08:00","id":1501457,"title":"","content":"I had my own piece of this, the Year of the Red Comet and the Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> THE WEEK OF NIGHTMARES Almost every Kindred Embraced in the 21st century has heard something about the Week of Nightmares, but most of them are fuzzy about the details. The ones who dwell in Cairo, despite being one of the most affected cities, are not much more in the clear, and possibly less.<br /> What basically everyone knows is that at some point at the beginning of the year 2000, a lot of Kindred starting seriously freaking out, killing each other in the process. The paranoia had started earlier, though, some say than during the second half of the 1990's. Gehena cults, millenarist prophets and apocalyptic texts had started popping out in Kindred society like mushrooms after heavy rain. In many cities around the world the Princes had decreed the hunting down of Caitiff and Thin-Bloods while the Sabbat had launched a large crusade in North America.<br /> Then, at the fall of 1999, a red star that could be seen only by Kindred , appeared on the skies, as an herald of impending doom. In Cairo a rumor that &quot;the last daughter of Eve&quot; was pregnant and hidden somewhere in the city, spread like wildfire, and many Kindred killed each other trying to find her before anyone else. Against the Prince's order, a rogue group started hunting the Thin-Bloods.<br /> Then came The Week. Because of its name, it seems clear that dreams and nightmares had to do with it. Whatever they dreamt of, Kindred started killing Kindred, scared senseless of the incoming arrival of the Antediluvians. Most likely many of the killers thought they would be saved if they followed the orders sent to them in dreams, or just tried to defend themselves against the ones who did.<br /> After one week the nightmares ended, but the millenarist hysteria grew. Everyone thought the Nightmares had been just the beginning of the end and the red star still hung defiantly in the nightly sky.<br /> Only it wasn't. Weeks, and then months went by and nothing happened. Of course, the Scourges still killed Thin-Bloods, the Sabbat kept fighting its apocalyptic north American crusade and the paranoid murdered anyone who approached them. But neither the Antediluvians nor Caine rose from their resting places and God didn't send the Wormwood to destroy the sinners. And suddenly, 369 nights after it had appeared, the red star left the sky without explanation. It took some time to readapt to the &quot;new normal&quot;, but it eventually happened. The Camarilla, which had presented itself as a bastion of calm and common sense, came up reinforced as an institution in Europe. In the Muslim world, the surviving Ashirra, many of whom had banded together against the most extremist Gehena cults, regained a sense of community that helped restore order and keep the Kindred society together. Eventually, the Sabbat, which for a time seemed to have triumphed in America, crumbled down and most of the cities it had conquered were taken back by the reinforced Camarilla.<br /> The final nail in the coffin for end of the world paranoids was the Inner Circle 2011 meeting. The Camarilla Elders issued a declaration merely mentioning the Year of the Herald and the Week of Nightmares as a &quot;freak event, followed by mass hysteria, that had endangered the Masquerade&quot; and issued a ban on both Gehena cults and the use of digital media, &quot;to avoid an irreversible misstep that would be fatal in these time of instantaneous worldwide communications&quot;. <br /> Additionally, to increase their ranks, Progeny creation rules were loosened a little, but the Accounting ones were tightened. The powers that be wanted to make sure the new generation of Neonates wouldn't fall into the rabbit hole of cults or conspiracy theories.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27429,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","user":"Microcuchon","date":". 01-27-2023, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T09:21:16-08:00","id":1501461,"title":"","content":"For my own personal Metaplot reboot has to start with the Sabbat and more specifically about the collapse of the Sabbat. I think the infernalism of Melinda Galbraith should be discovered and likewise the impersonation of Zachary Sikorsky. This sparks the final Sabbat Civil war with many cardinals trying to claim the Regency and using the Inquisition as a weapon saying each other is an infernalist. <br /> <br /> Eventually this leads to the Sabbat being weakened enough for the Camarilla to push into Sabbat territory. However this also leads to the Camarilla to be stretched thin in its resources and eventually having a massive independent movement which leads to a kind of &quot;neo war of princes&quot; where there are a whole bunch of new Vampire Nations that have old Sabbat and Camarilla with new Anarch ideas all mixed together banding together against other Vampire Nations.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T11:01:37-08:00","id":1501467,"title":"","content":"We went with the Sabbat crumbling when they learned that the Lasombra &amp; Tzismce antidulivans never suffered final death and that they wasted centuries fighting against monsters who barely cared what was happening with there progeny. When they did notice it was to stir the pot so to speak and they would spared further intrustions into whatever plans they had for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T03:19:51-08:00","id":1501523,"title":"","content":"I greatly toned down the damage to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> In my games, Melinda Galbraith started acting oddly, then disappeared. In her absence, the Sabbat was taken over by Cathari demagogues who increased in political power mainly by raising shovelheads to True Sabbat status in a small fraction of the time that other Paths did, basically as soon as the shovelhead displayed devotion to the Cathari path. The Cathari demagogues also generally encouraged reckless hedonism, which was destructive to the sect long term, but greatly appealed to the young, who viewed them as champions of freedom.<br /> <br /> This angered packs following the other Paths, but they were rapidly outnumbered.<br /> <br /> Eventually this cost the Sabbat several important cities because the Sabbat under the Cathari Demagogues was so sloppy. Nowhere near the collapse in canon, but enough that the Cathari were scrambling to spin this as a good thing, saying that the Sabbat were &quot;more dangerous than ever without territory&quot;, which many older Sabbat regarded as absolutely insulting propaganda.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat Inquisition made moves to take control of the Sabbat, using the cover of the Siege of New Orleans to establish New Orleans as the new capital of the Sabbat, abolishing the Regent position, and making the Grand Inquisitor the top Sabbat position. She then declared the Path of Cathari heretical and started a Civil War with the goal of genociding the Cathari Demagogues and their followers.<br /> <br /> Her ultimate goal has been to reforge the Sabbat as an alliance of those vampires who reject humanity, and to acquire a large territory with a safe border in which those vampires seeking to advance on Paths of Enlightment can do so in peace. The only vampires not welcome in this alliance of nonhuman religions are those whose beliefs are antithetical to the security of the Sabbat, such as Cathari, Evil Revelations, and Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T13:29:50-08:00","id":1501637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501429-metaplot-plot-thread-reboot?p=1501432#post1501432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is similar to what our gm has told us when we asked about our current plot where in our campaign the ucrain madness is basically GRU is deadly afraid of another vampire of calibre of baba yaga so they started this attrocity so they can draw out this millenia old vampire.<br /> <br /> Originally our GM had the idea that the ventrue prince of Trier who whas embraced back then in the second city made an alliance with the kiever rus by marrying the child of the prince of Kiew during 1000 who where embraced just to give him a wife. Now 1000 years later the fledgeling became a methusalah herself and sired daughters too. While the world may have forgotten the prince of trier still remembers the pledge he made. Now as the ukraine is oppressed he helps his with in supporting her that her eldest daughter could become the next prince of kiew and our characters who still had an undead debt to fullfill to him should go in there too and help her to become the winner in this fight and when there is chances help the oppressed population too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hailing from Trier makes this an extremely funny idea. (Trier is so small that it could sustain like.. 4 Cainites?)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also currently ST'ing a chronicle that's leading up to the 2000s and my PCs decided to join the Sabbat. The broad idea is that they'll be integral in the upcoming 4th Sabbat Civil War","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T04:26:20-08:00","id":1501689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501429-metaplot-plot-thread-reboot?p=1501637#post1501637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hailing from Trier makes this an extremely funny idea. (Trier is so small that it could sustain like.. 4 Cainites?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Depend on if you go by 10.000 People per Cainite or 100.000. If 100.000 then the city would actually be overpopulated with him being married. But we go by 10.000 and so the city would suitable for 11 cainites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T05:55:44-08:00","id":1501693,"title":"","content":"-Use of the information technology is increasing the spread of thaumaturgy among Anarchs and Sabbat. The Camarilla craves stability and obviously doesn't want this. Some Sabbat rites are also spreading among other sects. Owing to this, and the increasing pressure some neonates find themselves in, Infernalism is on the rise. <br /> <br /> -over the past decade many in the Camarilla and Sabbat have increasingly looked towards encouraging the spread of thaumaturgy specifically for it's mastery over technology, to mixed success. Control over technology has been recognized as key to the masquerade/ silence of the blood. Many cities have successfully lobbied to make the information needed to learn a limited selection of Thaumaturgy available to those in good standing (up to level 2) <br /> <br /> <br /> -The Camarilla is a truly Global organization. The Ashirra mostly formed to check Assamite/Baali agression, which became less necessary after the Tremere curse. While the Camarilla started in Europe as a response to the revolts and changes made by modernity, This spread rather naturally due to Colonialism +many elders from outside europe being offered incentives + Vampires not really caring much about human races because they go beyond biology + It actually being a good idea because modernity was spreading and Anarchs are a problem in any culture.<br /> <br /> -Cathayans exist but aren't as antagonistic. western equivalents exist but historically haven't had the population to create lasting societies. Between Hungry Ghosts and Vampires, Vampires have a big advantage in wars due to logistics, so they often push HG out of the cities. <br /> <br /> -Covid fucked over a lot of neonates, particularly Cassanova types. A hungry populace is a discontent one, and many political upsets happened in this period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T12:35:58-08:00","id":1501827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501429-metaplot-plot-thread-reboot?p=1501689#post1501689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depend on if you go by 10.000 People per Cainite or 100.000. If 100.000 then the city would actually be overpopulated with him being married. But we go by 10.000 and so the city would suitable for 11 cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how the 1 Kindred to 100,000 mortals guideline has ever worked in official publications, though. I don't know how many times I've seen people just look up city populations, apply the 1:100,000 ratio, come up with absurdly low vampire numbers, and conclude that the rule is junk. But the guideline is supposed to be used with the population numbers of metropolitan areas, including all the suburbs and hinterland surrounding a given city. The early <i>By Night</i> supplements were designed with this method in mind, so it's pretty obvious that the 1:100,000 ratio works just fine, especially if it is used (as intended) as a guideline and not a hard limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T11:22:00-08:00","id":1501892,"title":"","content":"I wonder how the other gamers work out the vampire population setting? Our city has just over a million people and we are trying to work out a good balance for an Anarch domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T11:36:11-08:00","id":1501893,"title":"","content":"That's one of those things that I think people overthink. Let the story be your guide. Are you telling a murder mystery that requires a dozen vampires? Then your city has a dozen vampires. Are you telling a war story that requires seven-plus gangs, each with seven-plus members? Then your city has fiftyish vampires. Let that be your guide rather than the 1 to 100,000 rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T13:07:32-08:00","id":1501902,"title":"","content":"100,000 humans for 1 Vampire? WTF that's way too low. I'd just go with 1000 humans for 1 Vampire like it suggests in one of the Vampire Dark Ages books (<i><b>Three Pillars</b></i>).<br /> <br /> With the 100,000 rule, supposedly a city like New York (EDIT: 8,000,000~ mortals) would only have 80 Vampires (LOL).... With 1000 humans for 1 Vampire rule, we'd get an accurate ballpark of 8000 &quot;official&quot; Vampires in NYC.<br /> <br /> Though like what others have said, these &quot;numbers&quot; for exact Vampire populations are just guidelines at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 02-01-2023, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T07:18:23-08:00","id":1501947,"title":"","content":"8000 vampires in one city is way too high. 80 vampires in one city seem way more inline with what I expect out of a city. 1:1000 only really make sense for the setting that that ratio comes from, Dark Ages, and that's only because the larger cities in that game are what like 15000 people? Even then I would probably exaggerate out the numbers to be something like ~20 vampires.<br /> <br /> My own rule of thumb is once you start getting into ~50 vampires then you are going to run into more masquerade breaches then you'd like to manage and if its more then 100 vampires then it becomes impossible to manage.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T10:00:21-08:00","id":1501958,"title":"","content":"Urban realities IE city planning/income inequality/crime rates/culture will have a big impact on how many vampires you can/should have. Something like the worst incarnation of Gotham or the city from Se7en could have 1:200 rate for vampires and still hold a reasonable grasp of the masquerade, while vampires in a utopian city might struggle to control aspects of the city with the few vampires they have. A single hellish prison could sustainably hold... I don't know, like 60 people per vampire <i>if we're conservative.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T10:21:18-08:00","id":1501960,"title":"","content":"While true there is also the aspect of <i>other vampires</i> not wanting all the competition for resources. If we are just talking survival then we can have 1:20 ratio to allow vampires a feeding rotation of their herd but, that is going to cause so much infighting that masquerade is out of the window.<br /> <br /> And that's really what I mean, like you <i>can</i> support way more vampires then 1:100k and have very few masquerade breaches just fine however, the greedy paranoid natures of vampires don't allow that many vampires to be around.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T11:30:50-08:00","id":1501963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501429-metaplot-plot-thread-reboot?p=1501947#post1501947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8000 vampires in one city is way too high. 80 vampires in one city seem way more inline with what I expect out of a city. 1:1000 only really make sense for the setting that that ratio comes from, Dark Ages, and that's only because the larger cities in that game are what like 15000 people? Even then I would probably exaggerate out the numbers to be something like ~20 vampires.<br /> <br /> My own rule of thumb is once you start getting into ~50 vampires then you are going to run into more masquerade breaches then you'd like to manage and if its more then 100 vampires then it becomes impossible to manage.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been to NYC numerous times. The entire place is HUGE (with a lot of verticality due to numerous high-rises and buildings in it), and so much goes on in a single <i>day</i> and <i>night </i>that doesn't get reported on, masquerade breaches would be easy for most Vampires to avoid. And you know how incompetent the NYPD is IRL, despite their budget being larger than many small countries' economies? Now imagine that in WoD, but in the 1990s (if your chronicle is active during that timeframe).<br /> <br /> I'd say that 80 Vampires in a large city like NYC would need MORE Vampires, just for the fact that trying to enforce praxis/authority in a city as large as NYC would be near impossible; you'd need more personnel to cover more ground in large city like NYC. If not, you'd basically have no authority to enforce anything and the other Vampires would just increase the population irregardless, as you'd have no power to make sure the others aren't just siring without your input. <br /> <br /> People say that Modern scenarios are harder for the Masquerade than Dark Age ones, but I'd disagree due to very fact that you mention; most Dark Age cities, despite the historically high populated ones, were small in number. People are more likely to pay attention to every small happening, along with the fact that curfews were common in most medieval cities. Once the gates closed for the night, it was very hard to leave and come back into and out. Not only that, unlike Modern cities, &quot;nightlife&quot; was near non-existent and most people almost always stayed in their homes for the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}